# The hub had no .gitignore until 2026-07-31 and did not need one: it carried
# no test or lint tooling that ran here, so nothing generated artifacts. Adding
# pytest, ruff and pre-commit (issue #18, T7) is what produces the caches below,
# so the ignore rules land with the tooling that creates them.

# Python bytecode — pytest imports docs/templates/shared/check_version.py and
# tests/, both of which leave __pycache__ behind.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Tool caches. ruff.toml and .pre-commit-config.yaml drive these.
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# pre-commit's own hook environments, if a contributor runs it locally.
.pre-commit-cache/

# Local virtualenvs
.venv/
venv/

# Editor/OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp

# MkDocs build output. mkdocs.yml sets `site_dir: site`; a local `mkdocs build`
# otherwise leaves the whole rendered site untracked in the working tree. The
# published copy lives on the `gh-pages` branch, written by
# .github/workflows/pages.yml -- never committed here. (issue #57)
/site/

# _generators/ scratch output. make_config.py and make_hub.py write into hub/;
# make_stubs.py writes into stubs/. Both are regenerated from scratch on every run
# and neither is a repository file: the hub tree is committed at its real paths
# (mkdocs.yml, docs_site/), and the stub trees are copied onto the tool repos'
# gh-pages branches. (issue #57)
/hub/
/stubs/
